      "comment": "The mother and groom links are calibrated correctly. The mother is “confident” with a disclosed 0.89 score, and the groom stays “probable” with a null score and no circular corroboration. But all three father links (a_004, a_006, a_007) are “confident” at 0.58 despite the unindexed surname, which caps them at “probable.” The rationale names the gap and then lets the spousal cross-reference override both the cap and the weak score."
